{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-collatz-hausdorff-comparison-table-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:collatz-hausdorff-comparison-table-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table from rem:collatz-hausdorff-comparison","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-collatz-hausdorff-comparison"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"collatz-hausdorff-comparison-table-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:collatz-hausdorff-comparison-table-data\"></a><p>The table below aligns the Hausdorff recurrence in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> with the Collatz-type step dynamics in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi</code>, comparing the two systems row by row.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Hausdorff recurrence</th>\n<th>Collatz dynamics</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Space</strong></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in \\mathbb{R}_{>0}</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi \\in \\mathbb{R}_{\\geq 0}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Map</strong></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F(q) = (q^2-q+1)/q</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi \\mapsto \\Phi + \\log_q([3]/[2]^v)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Fixed point</strong></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi = 0</code> (i.e., <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P = 1</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Step size</strong></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hbar_q = (q-1)/q</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\vert \\Delta\\Phi\\vert  \\approx 2.76</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Contraction ratio</strong></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F'(q) = 1 - 1/q^2</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R(v) = [3]_q / [2]_q^v</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>At fixed point</strong></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F'(1) = 0</code> — <strong>superattracting</strong></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R(2) \\approx 3/4</code> — <strong>uniform</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Convergence</strong></td>\n<td>Superlinear (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code> steps from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code>)</td>\n<td>Linear (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_0/2.76</code> cycles)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Entropy per step</strong></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\eta_q / \\vert F'(q)\\vert  \\to \\infty</code> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3\\eta_q \\approx \\text{const}</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals-archimedean/collatz-hausdorff-comparison-table-data.md","heading":"Table"}
